# Keep the build context tight. The Dockerfile selectively COPYs what it needs;
# this just reduces the context Docker sends to the daemon.

# Build outputs
**/target
**/*.bak

# VCS / editor
**/.git
**/.gitignore
**/.DS_Store
**/.vscode
**/.idea

# Dev-only docs are not part of the runtime image. Keep tools/ in the build
# context because Cargo metadata requires every workspace member to exist.
docs
DESIGN.md
README.md
LICENSE*
*.md

# Integration tests stay in the context because ci-rust cooks all targets.

# CI lives outside the build context
.woodpecker.yml
.dockerignore
Dockerfile
